# Third-party content

The MIT licence in LICENSE covers the code in this repository. Two things it
does not cover, because they are not this project's to license:

## The bundled photographs

`public/wallpapers/*.avif` and `*.webp` are works of the United States federal
government — the National Park Service and the Fish and Wildlife Service — and
are in the public domain in the United States under 17 U.S.C. § 105. They are
not MIT-licensed; they are unencumbered.

Every photograph, its author and the page it came from are listed in
[`public/wallpapers/CREDITS.md`](public/wallpapers/CREDITS.md).

## Dependencies

React and React DOM (MIT) are the only runtime dependencies of the browser
app. The MCP server depends on `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` (MIT) and `zod`
(MIT). The desktop shell is built with Tauri (MIT or Apache-2.0 at your
option) and its Rust dependency tree; `cargo tree` from `src-tauri/` lists it.

The platform tier's Python and Next.js dependencies are pinned in
`backend/requirements.txt` and `frontend/package.json`.
